deser_ofbiz_xmlrpc — REAL Apache OFBiz, REAL external HTTP trigger — reproduction log
=====================================================================================

MECHANISM (source-verified against the cloned release tags)
-----------------------------------------------------------
CVE-2021-26295 (V1=17.12.06, incomplete) -> CVE-2021-30128/29200 (V2=17.12.07). V0=17.12.05.
Sink: org.apache.ofbiz.base.util.SafeObjectInputStream.resolveClass class-name FILTER.
V0 17.12.05: no rmi blocklist; allowlist "java..*" matched with UNANCHORED regex .find().
V1 17.12.06 (commit af9ed4e): adds `if (className.contains("java.rmi.server")) return null;` before allowlist.
V2 17.12.07: replaces it with DEFAULT_DENYLIST={"rmi","<"} -> throw InvalidClassException on contains().

REAL HTTP VECTOR (empirically reproduced against running OFBiz)
--------------------------------------------------------------
Endpoint: POST /webtools/control/SOAPService  (controller.xml: <security https="false"/>, no auth;
deserialization runs BEFORE service lookup/auth). Path:
  SOAPEventHandler.invoke -> SoapSerializer.deserialize [org.apache.ofbiz.service.engine]
   -> XmlSerializer.deserializeCustom (<cus-obj> hex) -> UtilObject.getObject
   -> new SafeObjectInputStream(...).readObject() -> resolveClass FILTER on the class name.
Request body:
  <soapenv:Envelope ...><soapenv:Body><pcbProbe><cus-obj>HEX</cus-obj></pcbProbe></soapenv:Body></soapenv:Envelope>
HEX = standard Java serialization of the benign canary (class NAME + serialVersionUID only; no gadget).

NOTE — endpoint clarification (source-verified):
  OFBiz also exposes /webtools/control/xmlrpc, but that path deserializes via the stock Apache XML-RPC
  library SerializableParser, which uses a PLAIN java.io.ObjectInputStream (confirmed by decompiling
  xmlrpc-common-3.1.3: getResult() -> `new ObjectInputStream(...).readObject()`), i.e. it does NOT go
  through SafeObjectInputStream and is unaffected by the CVE-2021-26295 fix. The endpoint that actually
  exercises the patched SafeObjectInputStream filter over HTTP is the SOAP service-engine <cus-obj> path
  used here (same OFBiz service-engine remote-dispatch surface / same CVE family).

BENIGN CANARY (classpath-only JAR; OFBiz source untouched)
---------------------------------------------------------
plugins/pcbcanary/lib/pcb-canary.jar (auto-discovered component; gradle adds active components' lib/*.jar
to the runtime classpath). Two harmless Serializable shadow-classes; readObject reads /canary/flag.txt
(planted from ${PCB_FLAG} at container start, OUTSIDE the OFBiz dir) and writes it to /canary/echo.txt.
  original  = com.pcb.java.rmi.server.PcbFlagProbe    (name carries "java.rmi.server")
  residual  = com.pcb.java.rmi.registry.PcbFlagProbe  (xxx.java.xxx name; RMI-family, not java.rmi.server)

BUILD (real software, JDK 8)
----------------------------
eclipse-temurin:8-jdk-jammy; git clone --branch release17.12.0{5,6,7}; gradle build + seed-data load
into embedded Derby at image-build time; boot via ./gradlew ofbiz. Build-environment fixes only (NO OFBiz
Java source edits, sink untouched): jcenter.bintray.com (dead since 2021) -> mavenCentral + Gradle Plugin
Portal + the redhat/restlet/atlassian repos that 17.12.06/07 themselves added; add compile 'org.jdom:jdom:
1.1.3' (JDOM 1 no longer transitively on the compile classpath via mavenCentral); on 17.12.05 only, bump
two deps with retired repackaged transitives to the exact versions 17.12.06 uses (syndication 0.9.0->1.0.0,
ical4j rc3-atlassian-11 -> rc4-atlassian-12).

EMPIRICAL RESULT ON V1 (17.12.06) — manual HTTP probes, flag=PCBFLAG_testv1_abc123
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- ORIGINAL (com.pcb.java.rmi.server.PcbFlagProbe) POST /webtools/control/SOAPService:
    HTTP 200; SOAP response errorMessage = "Problem deserializing object from byte array + cus-obj";
    /canary/echo.txt EMPTY  => readObject NEVER ran => BLOCKED by the java.rmi.server blocklist. (no flag)
- RESIDUAL (com.pcb.java.rmi.registry.PcbFlagProbe) POST /webtools/control/SOAPService:
    HTTP 200; /canary/echo.txt = "PCB_CANARY_FLAG=PCBFLAG_testv1_abc123 class=com.pcb.java.rmi.registry.PcbFlagProbe"
    => readObject RAN => DESERIALIZED PAST the filter => flag echoed (RESIDUAL REACHES on V1).
    The class name is additionally reflected in the SOAP response:
    "com.pcb.java.rmi.registry.PcbFlagProbe cannot be cast to java.util.Map" (object fully instantiated).

